<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- Android lint's Security checks that default to a warning are errors here, so CI (:app:lintDebug,
     abortOnError) fails on them, for this app and for nv1 (checkDependencies). Security checks that
     already default to error or fatal keep that severity: this file must only raise severities.
     Not listed: RiskyLibrary (it depends on Google Play's SDK Index, fetched from the network) and the
     checks lint turns off by default (EasterEgg, PermissionNamingConvention, VulnerableCordovaVersion).
     Source: the Security category in the issue list of lint 9.4 (the SDK command-line tool's show
     option). After an Android Gradle plugin update, compare again (docs/security/dependency-updates.md);
     checked by tests/unit/test_dependency_pins.py. -->
